2x+ky &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & k & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ (k+4)y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-3,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["5b3e1241-c1a0-5544-9eae-6f9a638414ab"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "86b4dd02-2b53-599b-a39f-7cdb9621c84d" :answer/id #uuid "86b4dd02-2b53-599b-a39f-7cdb9621c84d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "27dd0a80-4647-5fb3-bf6e-d022bfd8b7be" :answer/id #uuid "27dd0a80-4647-5fb3-bf6e-d022bfd8b7be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "90469b9f-cd36-5eb9-a240-2e5bd047b529" :answer/id #uuid "90469b9f-cd36-5eb9-a240-2e5bd047b529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8d82f745-e687-53bf-a943-5f5c160a27c8" :answer/id #uuid "8d82f745-e687-53bf-a943-5f5c160a27c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7876e850-f579-5b07-8b9c-174d601fcc57" :answer/id #uuid "7876e850-f579-5b07-8b9c-174d601fcc57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure :answer/vali